our next guest is a two-time grammy  award-winning singer and songwriter and  now she's taking pen to paper with her  very first children's book the curly  girl blues everyone please  welcome tori kelly  um  speaking of grammys you're nominated for  two grammys  yes it's a huge huge honor i mean i  remember  being  nominated for the first time for best  new artists like when i was like me  artists and just starting out and it was  this whole like whirlwind of emotions  and that even that just trips me out it  was my childhood dream so the fact that  i like have those is just surreal to me  but  where did your grammys end up  so  so what people don't know  is you like you you go on stage and you  like accept the award and everything and  people think like that's your actual  grammy like you go home with that and  that's not true at all it's like just a  prop so like everyone's just holding the  same grammy and they like and they're  relevant right out of your hand yeah so  you walk off stage and you're like oh my  gosh and they're like thank you so much  and they just take it away  right what are you gonna do i thought  yeah  they send you the  grammys and the mail  like way later so this was like  months and months and months later and i  finally get like a notification  so they were like hey you weren't home  like we tried to deliver this package  and  uh  you know you weren't here so we sent  them to uh like the local drug store you  know you can like pick up just packages  and i we filmed the whole thing because  we thought it was so funny i'd be like  hey i think there's like two packages  here  like this big  they're gold yeah like golden  okay so you are nina insane  nina is such a meaningful  and important character in both movies  and  one of mina's story lines in sing too is  that she is with eric andre darius who's  like totally full of himself and  hilarious but she's not attracted to him  and they have to pretend like they're in  love  so  what happens pharrell is  another one of our amazing co-stars and  he  um he plays an elephant named alfonso  and that is who mina actually has a  crush on and it's so cute and so you  know by the end you're seeing  mina kind of picturing that it's him  instead of darius  uh and that kind of helps her get  through the performance because they  have a duet together and she's like how  am i supposed to pretend that i like  this guy so it's really sweet i love her  storyline in in this movie  i i really also love the fact that you  did not with the grammys and the  starring roles in the big franchise  movies  that is not exactly where your story  started and for me i always like to  laugh and i love the lighter side of  life but i like the depth too what was  the struggle what was the journey like  it wasn't always easy for you  it wasn't no i um  basically you know i mean i went into  record labels and i was like 12 years  old i did  a ton of different like competition tv  shows and you know got a lot of  rejection along the way nothing was  panning out and finally i was like  you know what i've gotten all these no's  i'm gonna just  kind of  take my career into my own hands and  that's when i started just posting  videos online on youtube and just like  doing covers with friends and like  picking up the guitar and just i was  just having so much fun with it i didn't  care anymore like who  was watching and slowly but surely  it you know people started noticing and  i started getting to do shows  and  it's been amazing i mean i think  i think without all of that rejection at  such a young age i mean you know maybe i  wouldn't have had that same like drive  and that same fire  to be able to you know do what i'm doing  now even and your curly girl blues  inspired  um from your own childhood yeah  tell me about that yeah so i  have curly hair and i did not like it  growing up you know at school and stuff  i didn't really see like my hair and i  was very insecure about it and  i wanted to write a book that could  hopefully inspire other kids you know if  i went through this and i didn't like my  hair and was struggling with it you know  there's got to be other kids who also  you know could spoil the same way once  again you took your discomfort and  turned it into your empowerment and  those messages resonate with people they  resonate with me  um so much um as a last question may i  ask you is it true that you were pen  pals with your husband  we were yeah it was very it just wasn't  like flirty at all in the beginning we  were just like writing to each other on  like different sides of the world and  then for like five months we were doing  that and we finally met and it was like  wow we like each other  long story short well i think that goes  to show us all keep writing everybody  it's such an amazing way to communicate  as is writing a children's book head to  the curlygirlblues.com  [Applause]  to get your amazing copy of this amazing  book  [Music]
 

